OL,3,GNEWSAInside the Shakespeare archive at
OL,4,Athe centre of a growing row
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn a library in Stratford-upon-Avon
OL,7,Fsits a collection of annotated scripts,
OL,8,Frehearsal notes, stage designs, letters
OL,9,Fand photographs that chart decades of
OL,10,FBritain's theatrical history.
OL,12,FIts shelves hold traces of actors,
OL,13,Fdirectors and productions that have
OL,14,Fshaped how generations have understood
OL,15,FShakespeare's work.
OL,17,FMost visitors to the town come for the
OL,18,Fplaywright's birthplace or the Royal
OL,19,FShakespeare Company (RSC). Few will
OL,20,Fever see the archive housed at the
OL,21,FShakespeare Institute.
